Alex, on the proposal of LOG.md §6: "好根据你的建议，下一步". So the writer's rule stays, and he asks for the next step.

Facts read today, all on saved data:
- The clean system's seeded end-to-end result (`e2e-2026-11-09/stage2-result.txt`): 18, 18, 17 agreements against production's 17, 15,
  16. The clean misses are q12 in all three draws (capital spending, a known Step 1 gap, D394), q17 in draw 3 and q22 in draw 2
  (FY2028 revenue, which sits on a rung boundary in every draw). None is traced to Step 2.
- Step 2's three lines were met at the acceptance of 2026-11-09 (search 141 of 143, clear wrong merges 1 of 57, later details kept).
- Of everything the judge was shown in the three draws, 31% to 35% is a second or later copy of a statement already shown in the
  same request (1,536 of 4,575 items in draw 1; up to 14 copies of one statement; requests of up to 89 items). This follows Alex's
  decision of 2026-11-08 (each repeat keeps its own text) as the experimental adapter delivers it: every copy its own item with an
  "Opinion, not verified: same claim as …" line. PRD §6 says "How a judgement reads a group is being tested"; no test with the
  judge exists.
- Step 4 (the ladder step) is in another session's hands and is where the end-to-end misses of the unseeded run come from.

My lean: Step 2 closes here, as Step 1 closed on c8: its lines are met and no end-to-end miss is traced to it. The one piece of its
hand-off never tested where the product is judged is how the judge reads repeats. The cheapest decisive check is a sizing: for a
few last-day judgements with the most copies, send the request as saved and with each statement shown once, three answers each,
and compare the conclusion and the input size. If the conclusion holds, design a delivery of one entry a statement (keeping what a
later copy adds); if it does not, the copies carry weight and stay. A hand-edited request is a sizing, not a product path, and
must be labelled so. Against it: production's attempt to shorten what the judge reads (argument records, judging-v8 and v9,
2026-11-04) failed, though that changed the judge and this changes only the list; and it may be a small matter beside Step 4.
